    "Weighted accuracy dropped from 0.997992 (AS-SET-03) to 0.993263 (AS-SET-04)",
    "Hangul accuracy dropped from 99.748% to 99.076% (-0.67%p, 8 broken rows)",
    "Non-Hangul accuracy slightly dropped from 99.918% to 99.909% (1 fixed, 2 broken)",
    "All 8 broken Hangul rows belong to two sister-ship groups: '모닝 피스' (Fold 3, 4 rows) and '우찬' (Fold 4, 4 rows)"
  ],
  "interpretations": [
    "train.py's 80% hardness heuristic (max(ratio, phone_ratio) - 0.5*gap) explicitly mines confusing sister-ships into the candidate pool.",
    "Removing Hard Negative Mining caused the training candidate pool to be dominated by easy negatives (similar tonnage, but dissimilar names).",
    "Without training on hard negative sister-ships, SetDecisionModel loses fine-grained discriminative power between sister vessels at inference.",
    "Therefore, candidate alignment alone cannot omit Hard Negative Mining; maintaining hard negatives in training is structurally essential."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Development G5 evaluation only; no Public test estimate",
    "User-authorized Python 3.11.15 execution",
    "Compares exact candidate selection algorithm alignment"
  ],
